      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to [[credential-scoping]], the Anthropic API key is **injected into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process, immediately before that process starts**. \n\nThe key points are:\n\n1. The Hub process itself **never holds** the API key in its own process environment\n2. A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n3. The key is injected **only into the child process** that needs it (either the Ingest or Query agent)\n4. The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated with the credential\n5. This design prevents a compromised or misbehaving Hub process from leaking the credential by inspecting environment variables\n\nThe same scoping model applies to the Query agent as well\u2014it also receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn time.",
